d Assist with financial aid workshops, Open Houses, and other events as needed Other general office duties as assigned Typical Qualifications 2.5 cumulative GPA (3.0 or better preferred) Interpersonal communication skills Ability to maintain confidential student information Reliability and punctuality Appropriate dress and professional behavior and attitude required Current enrollment as a GSU student Supplemental Information Applicants must include a letter of interest, current resume/employment application, and names and contact information for at least three references. Apply online at http://agency.governmentjobs.com/glenvilleedu/default.cfm . Glenville State University is proud of its commitment to affirmative action. Women, members of minorities and people with disabilities are encouraged to apply. Employer Glenville State University Address 200 High Street Glenville, West Virginia, 26351 Phone (304) 462-6193 Website http://www.glenville.edu Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Job Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assistance, please email privacy@neogov.com × Accessibili