      "description": "Job Opportunities | Open Positions at For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser GSU Student Position- Student Activities Board Member | Open Positions at  page has loaded. GSU Student Position- Student Activities Board Member | Open Positions at  page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Job Opportunities Menu Job Opportunities Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. Open Positions at powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" GSU Student Position- Student Activities Board Member Print Apply ﻿ GSU Student Position- Student Activities Board Member Salary $8.75 Hourly Location 200 High Street, Glenville, WV Job Type Non-classified Job Number 0485TWS025 Division Student Life Opening Date 09/11/2026 Description The Office of Student Life is seeking a variety of student workers to be key members of the campus life and engagement team. As a member of the Student Activities Board, students will engage with the student body to help both plan and implement a wide variety of events on behalf of the Office of Student Life. The events will be both standalone events and collaborative events with other campus offices and student organizations. The Student Activities Board members will represent the interests of the entire GSU student body while getting hands on experience in communication, budgeting, marketing, and interpersonal relationships. Examples of Duties Assist with setup, breakdown, registration, and hosting of campus events (Homecoming, movie nights, guest speakers, tournaments, social activities, and more). Participate in required team meetings and brainstorming sessions to foster unique event ideas that promotes a vibrant campus culture. Create promotional materials, assist with social media outreach, and distribute flyers across campus to boost student attendance. Serve as a friendly, approachable representative of the Office of Student Life and the Student Activities Board to students, faculty, staff, and visitors. Help maintain, organize, and store event supplies and equipment. Maintain student confidentiality when handling event sign-ins and abide by all University and Student Life policies and procedures. Typical Qualifications Currently enrolled as a degree-seeking GSU student. Minimum 2.50 cumulative GPA required; 3.0 or higher preferred. Strong interpersonal communication, customer service, and teamwork skills. Punctual, proactive, and capable of managing event logistics while maintaining professional behavior and appropriate attire. Willingness to work evening and weekend hours based on the event schedule. Prior experience in event planning, graphic design, social media marketing, or student leadership preferred but not required. While prior experience isn’t required, enthusiasm is. Along with your application, please include a letter stating why you would like to be a member of the Student Activities Board. Supplemental Information Applicants must include a letter of interest, current resume/employment application, and names and contact information for at least three references. Apply online at http://agency.governmentjobs.com/glenvilleedu/default.cfm . Glenville State University is proud of its commitment to affirmative action. Women, members of minorities and people with disabilities are 